{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts","id":1286172,"title":"Speculating on God-Blooded Exalts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-09T07:12:16-08:00","id":1286172,"title":"Speculating on God-Blooded Exalts","content":"Had a bit of a brainstorm on how I'd handle God-Blooded Exalts, and similarly divine inheritances.<br /> <br /> <b>Rareified Inheritance (\u2022\u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) \u2014 Innate</b><br /> The character descends from a potent supernatural being, and can draw upon that heritage in myriad ways.<br /> <br /> Characters with this Merit may purchase Evocations, representing the influence of their parentage. In general, more potent supernatural lineages and closer relations will allow access to more powerful Evocations, but such things are not certain; most God-Blooded children have nothing more than a wispy trace of the divine made manifest in them, while others may suddenly come into a blood of power they never knew from a long distant ancestor.<br /> <br /> Mortals with this merit gain a personal mote pool of 10 motes, and are treated as having Essence 1 for the purpose of any Evocations making use of her Essence. Exalts and other characters who naturally have Essence do not gain this benefit.<br /> <br /> <i>What about the Golden Children, the Moon-Touched, and the Star-Kissed?</i><br /> <br /> The power of Celestial Exaltation is generally too potent to be transferred through the blood. Even so, the children of the Solars, Lunars, and Sidereals often bear clear marks of their heritage, and a small number inherit a small measure of their parents power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T07:58:21-08:00","id":1286179,"title":"","content":"You don't need to treat mortals as having essence 1. They really do have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T08:00:12-08:00","id":1286180,"title":"","content":"Well, i did think of about the same thing - using the artifact &amp; evocations system to portray god-blooded Inheritance as a whole, a few years ago.<br /> Kind of a natural step for one to house rule things into when one thinks of the &quot;background/merit parity&quot; and such stuff, i guess.<br /> <br /> It also lead me to the idea of keeping the heritages separate, unlike in previous editions, much like artifacts don't (usually, inadvertently) gel into one super-artifact just because.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286179#post1286179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to treat mortals as having essence 1. They really do have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the OP's point is focused more on the matter of being able to channel essence in artifact use, much like an Ess 1 exalt/spirit/etc, but unlike your run-of-the-mill mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-09-2019, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T08:49:54-08:00","id":1286197,"title":"","content":"For God-Blooded Exalted, what about something like...say, a Merit (call it Divine Inheritance or something) that allows the Exalt the potential to learn up to one spirit Charm per dot? (Only for Charms appropriate to their divine parent, and they would still have to spend XP or starting Charm picks on the actual Charms.)<br /> <br /> Probably it would allow the Exalt to learn powers and traits on par with what a Solar might have learned by devouring their divine parent with Carnal Spirit Rending. (If someone wants to learn &quot;greater miracles&quot; as referenced in Divine Mantle, it should probably cost more than one dot each, if you'd allow that for a God-Blood at all. I'm not sure I would.)<br /> <br /> I don't know if this is really balanced. I'm pretty sure any effect that allows the Exalted to learn spirit powers is going to require a lot of case-by-case balancing, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T09:03:32-08:00","id":1286203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts#post1286172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Characters with this Merit may purchase Evocations, representing the influence of their parentage.<br /> <br /> <br /> In general, more potent supernatural lineages and closer relations will allow access to more powerful Evocations, but such things are not certain; most God-Blooded children have nothing more than a wispy trace of the divine made manifest in them, while others may suddenly come into a blood of power they never knew from a long distant ancestor.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... is an incredible idea in its simplicity, its scope, and its versatility while also not being something that can be wildly too powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T10:31:51-08:00","id":1286217,"title":"","content":"We might need to add rules for getting essence higher than one, mind you, cos one of the canon godblooded is essence 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T10:44:45-08:00","id":1286222,"title":"","content":"While I think yours is elegant in its simplicity, but apparently we will be getting some official rules here soon:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1285443#post1285443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God-blooded Exalted will be discussed in Heirs to the Shogunate \u2014 a bit earlier than we'd expected, but between Ledaal Kebok Coren and Clan Akatha, we just had to.<br /> <br /> We're planning to address god-blooded more generally in future books.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page1035\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-devs/page1035</a></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","user":"Snakesandsuns","date":". 02-09-2019, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T12:07:08-08:00","id":1286255,"title":"","content":"Feel up to statting up an example of one of these to sort of better feel around how it would work in practice? Grab a sig Godblooded DB or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T15:13:56-08:00","id":1286295,"title":"","content":"One issue that came up in 2e was that, if you create a merit that increases the general power level of a character, it becomes a \u201cmust buy\u201d and distorts the game. Defining Rarified Inheritance as a trait that god blooded just get at a specific rating, depending on desired power level, rather than something they buy with merit dots would be less prone to abuse.<br /> <br /> Like, I think it would work fine as a merit for an Exalt, because it\u2019s basically a reskin of the Artifact merit. However, if you have a group of God Blooded PCs, having this as a merit they have to buy is either a tax to soak up their merit dots or a trap they can accidentally fall into. Either way, if they don\u2019t all buy the same level, you can end up with characters who have vastly different amounts of power, which is problematic if not done on purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 02-09-2019, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T15:21:58-08:00","id":1286297,"title":"","content":"The most balanced way to do a Solar (or, possibly, Lunar) Godblood with spirit charms is to play an Eclipse and take some Eclipse-okay spirit charms at character gen, representing your heritage.<br /> <br /> You already know the powers are balanced yet iconic.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's not much good if you're a Zenith or a Fire Aspect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T18:59:41-08:00","id":1286340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286297#post1286297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most balanced way to do a Solar (or, possibly, Lunar) Godblood with spirit charms is to play an Eclipse and take some Eclipse-okay spirit charms at character gen, representing your heritage.<br /> <br /> You already know the powers are balanced yet iconic.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's not much good if you're a Zenith or a Fire Aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could always take Divine Mantle with a Principle of &quot;I want to be just like my dad!&quot; Then you're not limited to Eclipse-okay Charms (or to being an Eclipse).<br /> <br /> ...I'm really surprised the writers went to the trouble of marking appropriate spirit Charms as Eclipse-okay, and then added Charms by which Solars could get access to other spirit Charms anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T19:27:16-08:00","id":1286345,"title":"","content":"Well, it's not exactly like they are easy to pick up, plus the ST still has to approve them for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T19:40:05-08:00","id":1286347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286217#post1286217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We might need to add rules for getting essence higher than one, mind you, cos one of the canon godblooded is essence 3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which character is that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T19:53:25-08:00","id":1286350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286255#post1286255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feel up to statting up an example of one of these to sort of better feel around how it would work in practice? Grab a sig Godblooded DB or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try and put together a stab (heh) at Ledaal Kebok Coren using Stormcaller- plus, I hadn't thought about how Resonant/Dissonant concepts would work within this framework. Gonna take a think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T19:56:06-08:00","id":1286351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286295#post1286295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One issue that came up in 2e was that, if you create a merit that increases the general power level of a character, it becomes a \u201cmust buy\u201d and distorts the game. Defining Rarified Inheritance as a trait that god blooded just get at a specific rating, depending on desired power level, rather than something they buy with merit dots would be less prone to abuse.<br /> <br /> Like, I think it would work fine as a merit for an Exalt, because it\u2019s basically a reskin of the Artifact merit. However, if you have a group of God Blooded PCs, having this as a merit they have to buy is either a tax to soak up their merit dots or a trap they can accidentally fall into. Either way, if they don\u2019t all buy the same level, you can end up with characters who have vastly different amounts of power, which is problematic if not done on purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>True; on the other hand, because the Essence and motes don't increase with more merit dots (only the potential power of the evocations), it's less impactful than Inheritance aka the Background That Keeps Giving (more backgrounds).<br /> <br /> And I'm more interested in finding a solution for Exalted godblooded that can also work as a way to stat up NPCs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T20:01:44-08:00","id":1286353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286297#post1286297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most balanced way to do a Solar (or, possibly, Lunar) Godblood with spirit charms is to play an Eclipse and take some Eclipse-okay spirit charms at character gen, representing your heritage.<br /> <br /> You already know the powers are balanced yet iconic.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's not much good if you're a Zenith or a Fire Aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286340#post1286340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could always take Divine Mantle with a Principle of &quot;I want to be just like my dad!&quot; Then you're not limited to Eclipse-okay Charms (or to being an Eclipse).<br /> <br /> ...I'm really surprised the writers went to the trouble of marking appropriate spirit Charms as Eclipse-okay, and then added Charms by which Solars could get access to other spirit Charms anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I *hate* Divine Mantle. Like, with the burning hatred of a thousand suns. Neat concept, dangerous idea, poor execution. (I don't hate it as much as Doombot-the-Charm or Lore-Lol-Meteor-Strike, but... it's in my top ten 'needs improvement')<br /> <br /> That said, Eclipse-OK charms are one solution, but they don't generalize to the God-Blooded children of Exalts (the Golden Children, the Moon-Touched, and the... Star-Kissed, I think?), nor (probably) the Fae-blooded.<br /> <br /> Plus, this way, every cool artifact doubles up as a way to create a cool godblooded character!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T22:33:44-08:00","id":1286366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286351#post1286351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True; on the other hand, because the Essence and motes don't increase with more merit dots (only the potential power of the evocations), it's less impactful than Inheritance aka the Background That Keeps Giving (more backgrounds).<br /> <br /> And I'm more interested in finding a solution for Exalted godblooded that can also work as a way to stat up NPCs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe split it into two then? Keep Rarefied Inheritance as the Not!Artifact Merit and just say that God Blooded who have actual charms get 10m per dot of Essence, so it's not specifically part of the merit. And maybe include a suggestion that the ST just give everyone a specific rating in it, when playing a God Blooded game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T00:49:51-08:00","id":1286380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286353#post1286353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I *hate* Divine Mantle. Like, with the burning hatred of a thousand suns. Neat concept, dangerous idea, poor execution. (I don't hate it as much as Doombot-the-Charm or Lore-Lol-Meteor-Strike, but... it's in my top ten 'needs improvement')<br /> <br /> That said, Eclipse-OK charms are one solution, but they don't generalize to the God-Blooded children of Exalts (the Golden Children, the Moon-Touched, and the... Star-Kissed, I think?), nor (probably) the Fae-blooded.<br /> <br /> Plus, this way, every cool artifact doubles up as a way to create a cool godblooded character!</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a very poorly written charm, although not literally the worst, IMO.<br /> But bad.<br /> <br /> Fae have some Eclipse-ok charms, so that's fine.<br /> <br /> Children of Exalts... Well, Moon-Children I think are better represented by high attributes, supernatural merits, and stuff like &quot;You can turn into your parent's spirit shape for 1wp.&quot;<br /> Giving them Lunar charms would be broken.<br /> Golden children are irrelevant because babies don't need stats.<br /> Star-children... No idea, but giving them Sidereal charms seems like a bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T03:47:48-08:00","id":1286403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286347#post1286347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which character is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fivefold Masks and Lies, from Adversaries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T03:50:46-08:00","id":1286404,"title":"","content":"Also, I think the easiest thing to do is say that exalts can just take this, but for mortals it's very much only with ST approval.<br /> <br /> Because as far as empowerment goes, it's not that much more of a jump than getting sorcery is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T05:27:20-08:00","id":1286417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286380#post1286380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Golden children are irrelevant because babies don't need stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there had been <i>zero</i> Solars around in the thousand-plus years since the Usurpation, I'd agree with this logic.<br /> <br /> As it stands, one of the Solar PCs in my Okeanos game was also the son of another Solar, who had perished tragically in a Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> (Fact is, <i>every</i> PC in that game ended up being <i>some</i> stripe of [X]-Blooded or [X]-Touched.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T05:46:42-08:00","id":1286418,"title":"","content":"Admittedly, you are right. It's very unlikely to come up, but it's possible, especially in a long game (in-character).<br /> <br /> But presumably, a Solar who is the son of a Solar needs no special rules.<br /> <br /> How did you handle all the X-blooded, mechanically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T07:18:24-08:00","id":1286428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286366#post1286366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe split it into two then? Keep Rarefied Inheritance as the Not!Artifact Merit and just say that God Blooded who have actual charms get 10m per dot of Essence, so it's not specifically part of the merit. And maybe include a suggestion that the ST just give everyone a specific rating in it, when playing a God Blooded game?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think anyone is going to have Essence now without innately having something to spend it on, which makes divorcing the two kinda weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T08:44:55-08:00","id":1286457,"title":"","content":"Actually, that's a point. At the moment it doesn't give mortals anything to spend motes on by itself. Maybe it should come with a free evocation? <br /> <br /> I mean, a lot of artifacts do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T10:53:09-08:00","id":1286490,"title":"","content":"Doesn't it seem weird for, say, the daughter of a fire-god to have the supernatural power to unlock the power of magic weapons?<br /> <br /> Rather than, say, the power to shoot fire, manipulate fire, and not be hurt by fire.<br /> <br /> And how many god-blooded even have a magic weapon anyway?<br /> <br /> Similarly, if you're a Solar who is the child of a storm-god, then letting you buy evocations... well, you could do that already.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T11:39:00-08:00","id":1286499,"title":"","content":"They're not, y'know <i>actually</i> evocations. They're charms. We're just calling them evocations cos we're treating the inheritance like an artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T11:51:48-08:00","id":1286502,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... yeah, that works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T13:33:48-08:00","id":1286526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286418#post1286418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But presumably, a Solar who is the son of a Solar needs no special rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, for the same reason I feel having lived your entire life on a Fire-aspected demesne should have an impact on a character, even if he Exalts as a Fire Aspect. The presence of potent Essence has a tendency in-setting to wreak changes on those in proximity to it, and having .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286418#post1286418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did you handle all the X-blooded, mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>I left the option open for them to develop unique Charms representing their unique heritage, though admittedly the players never took me up on it. I also let them take Merits that seemed appropriate to their heritage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-10-2019, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T15:22:44-08:00","id":1286551,"title":"","content":"So, here is a stab at Ledaal Kebok Coren: Recent graduate from the House of Bells, descendant of the storm demon Yan, who frightens her own house with her skill with the blade and that the sky itself darkens with her anger.<br /> <br /> She uses Rarefied Inheritance to gain the Evocations of Stormcaller, from Arms of the Chosen, to represent her descent from Yan- with some tweaks for how Intensity is generated / what the purification ritual is about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/2697\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/2697\" target=\"_blank\"> Ledaal Kebok Coren | Lot-Casting Atemi </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/2697\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.lotcastingatemi.com/characters/2697 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Online Character and Chronicle manager for Exalted Third Edition. Supports all published Exalt types, mortals, and homebrew exalt types. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T03:43:44-08:00","id":1286652,"title":"","content":"Recommendations:<br /> <br /> 1. Specify explicitly that the merit rating is equivalent to that of an artifact for determining the quantity and power of the Evocations you can derive from your nature.<br /> <br /> 2. You're resonant with Evocations from your heritage because duh.<br /> <br /> 3. Mortals with the merit can raise their permanent Essence rating, to a maximum of the merit rating, using the XP table for Solars.<br /> <br /> 4. Mortal mote pool is 10*Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T03:53:28-08:00","id":1286653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286652#post1286652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Recommendations:<br /> <br /> 1. Specify explicitly that the merit rating is equivalent to that of an artifact for determining the quantity and power of the Evocations you can derive from your nature.<br /> <br /> 2. You're resonant with Evocations from your heritage because duh.<br /> <br /> 3. Mortals with the merit can raise their permanent Essence rating, to a maximum of the merit rating, using the XP table for Solars.<br /> <br /> 4. Mortal mote pool is 10*Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For 3--You mean mortals automatically increase their essence like Solars right? Because I don't think you can just buy essence anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T03:53:37-08:00","id":1286654,"title":"","content":"Definitely agree with all of these, except maybe number 2. Just don't bother with resonance/dissonance.<br /> <br /> (Maybe also mention that inheritance 1 and 2 are, like, a <i>thing</i>, but better represented by individual merits.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T03:56:34-08:00","id":1286655,"title":"","content":"Not only is the distinction irrelevant since there are no Artifacts to transfer between different kinds of owner, I would propose that the kinds of bonus that powers can have from Resonance might be a bit too strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T07:14:00-08:00","id":1286697,"title":"","content":"<b>Rarefied Inheritance (\u2022\u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) \u2014 Innate</b><br /> The character descends from a potent supernatural being, and can draw upon that heritage in myriad ways.<br /> <br /> Characters with this Merit may purchase Evocations, representing the influence of their parentage. In general, more potent supernatural lineages and closer relations will allow access to more powerful Evocations, but such things are not certain; most God-Blooded children have nothing more than a wispy trace of the divine made manifest in them, while others may suddenly come into a blood of power they never knew from a long distant ancestor.<br /> <br /> Mortals with this merit should note their Permanent Essence as 1, and gain a personal mote pool of 10 motes per point of Permanent Essence. They increase in Permanent Essence at the same rate as a Solar, to a maximum Permanent Essence of 3. Exalts and other characters who naturally have Essence do not increase their Essence pools. <br /> <br /> When considering the strength of the Evocations granted, Mortals are always resonant with the Evocations granted by this merit. Celestial Exaltation, such as the Solars, Lunars, and Sidereals, tends to overwhelm these lesser gifts- when they manifest, the character is naturally dissonant with them. Terrestrial Exaltation, carried as it is in the blood, is more accommodating and treats the character as neither resonant nor dissonant to these gifts. While the gifts of Rarefied Inheritance cannot be transferred from one bearer to another as Artifacts can, these are useful benchmarks when either adapting existing Evocations or creating new ones.<br /> <br /> Rarefied Inheritance is not the only way that supernatural ancestry manifests; often, it is no more than an unusual feature, such as a peculiar hair or eye color, or is better represented with other Merits that provide innate advantages, such as Boundless Endurance, Danger Sense, Fast Reflexes, Giant; or by supernatural merits such as Enhanced Sense, Exalted Healing, or Wings.<br /> <br /> <i>What about the Golden Children, the Moon-Touched, and the Star-Kissed?</i><br /> <br /> The power of Celestial Exaltation is generally too potent to be transferred through the blood. Even so, the children of the Solars, Lunars, and Sidereals often bear clear marks of their heritage, and a small number inherit a small measure of their parents power.<br /> <br /> (Which does mean that Ledaal Kebok Coren needs to be adjusted a bit, but only slightly)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 02-11-2019, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T19:15:17-08:00","id":1286946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286654#post1286654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely agree with all of these, except maybe number 2. Just don't bother with resonance/dissonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I didn\u2019t literally mean to include irrelevant keywords, just that the Evocations should be of resonant-equivalent strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T23:14:33-08:00","id":1286982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1286172-speculating-on-god-blooded-exalts?p=1286946#post1286946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I didn\u2019t literally mean to include irrelevant keywords, just that the Evocations should be of resonant-equivalent strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree; Resonant Evocations tend to be pretty damned potent. I'd be cautious giving that power level to God-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T05:06:04-08:00","id":1287023,"title":"","content":"Subject to strength / balance concerns, using resonant as a smoothing property between Celestial-&gt;Terrestrial-&gt;Mortals with divine blood is quite a nice and elegant design. <br /> <br /> Consonant with the setting information, and should have some interesting, not imbalancing play properties, where edges from Godblood are most significant for mortals, closer to neat but small and not overwhelming edges for Celestials and intermediate for Dragonblooded (and I guess also offset some of the potential for synergies between 'native' edges and divine blood that could end up making Celestial godblooded stronger than they ought to be compared to other Celestials and other kinds of godblooded?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-12T05:15:25-08:00","id":1287025,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting idea, but personally I still just wouldn't bother with the distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}